 "lineage_rule": "A lineage is one unit for partitioning. Models are the same lineage if one is a size variant, fine-tune, distillation or derivative of another, if they share pretrained weights (including a pretrained sub-network such as a text encoder or backbone), or if a model explicitly adopts another family's architecture and tokenizer (e.g. TinyLlama adopts Llama 2's). Training and inference uses of one lineage always go to the same partition. For non-ML work a lineage is an application family (e.g. all RAPIDS libraries are one unit).",
